-- title:
--   Evaluation at a place extends to the completed node ring
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a level $N\ge 1$, a field $k$ of characteristic $q$ that is perfect, a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red}\colon A\to k$, modular polynomial data for $q$ satisfying the Kronecker congruence $\Phi \equiv (X^{q}-Y)(X-Y^{q})$ modulo $q$, integrality of the Hecke correspondence maps $\bar\alpha$, $\bar\beta$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at level $N$ and prime $q$, and a place specialization $P$ for these data. Let $R$ be a prolongation tuple for $P$, let $K$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$, let $w$ be a place of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\ k\ N$ over $k$, and write $B=R.\mathrm{nodeIntegersOver}\ K\ w$ for the subring of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}(Nq)$ of those $f$ lying in $R.\mathrm{nodeIntegers}\ w$ whose Laurent series lies in $\mathrm{NodeLocalized.fieldOver}\ (Nq)\ K$. Let $c$ be a system of node coordinates at $w$: elements $x,y\in B$ with $x$ killed by the first node residue and of order $1$ for the second residue measured at the Frobenius translate $\mathrm{arithFrobC}\,q\,k\,N\cdot w$, and $y$ killed by the second node residue and of $w$-order $1$ for the first. Let $\varpi$ be a nonzero element of $A\cap K$, assume $B$ is local with maximal ideal generated by the constant function $\varpi$ together with $x$ and $y$, and assume the value integrality law at $w$: every $f\in R.\mathrm{nodeIntegers}\ w$ has $V.\mathrm{evalAt}\ f\in A$ for all places $V$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}(Nq)$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\ V=w$. Then for each such $V$ (i.e. with $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\ V=w$) there is a ring homomorphism $\psi$ from the $\mathfrak m_B$-adic completion of $B$ to the valuation ring $\mathcal O$ of the completion of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ for the valuation of $A$, which is a local homomorphism, and which satisfies $\psi(\hat g)=V.\mathrm{evalAt}\ g$ in that completion for every $g\in B$, where $\hat g$ is the canonical image of $g$.
--
--   This provides, at a node of the reduction of $X_0(Nq)$ described by the coordinates $x,y$, a local homomorphism from the completed local ring of the node into the valuation ring of the completed algebraic numbers extending evaluation at a place $V$ above $w$; equivalently, it realises $V$ as a point of the formal neighbourhood of the node. It is used in the lemmas bounding the number of places above $w$ and relating node depths to valuations of evaluated coordinates.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_PlaceSpecialization_ProlongationTuple_exists_ringHom_adicCompletion_nodeIntegersOver_comp_eq_evalAt.lean

